## Description

Surface `TEST-NNNNNN` dev-artifact nodes (from `STEP-000003-UVqkd7cL`) in
the VS Code Chain Inspector: a "Tests" sub-section under "Dev Artifacts",
a passing/failing/blocked/proposed status glyph, a dedicated icon, and
nesting under both a test's parent requirement and its parent step — the
UI half of `REQ-000011-UVqkd7cL`.

## Actions performed

- `packages/catalyst-host-vscode/src/tree.ts`: added a nested "Tests"
  sub-section under the "Dev Artifacts" section grouping, and a
  dedicated status-glyph branch for a test's
  passing/failing/blocked/proposed status (the generic dev-artifact
  fallback didn't distinguish these).
- `packages/catalyst-host-vscode/src/extension.ts`: added a dedicated
  icon for the `"test"` dev-artifact kind, and extended
  `ChainInspectorProvider`'s requirement/step child-resolution methods
  (`hasStepChildren`/`stepChildrenFor`-style helpers) to also resolve a
  test's parent requirement and parent step via `model.reverseEdges`, so
  a test nests under both wherever it names them (many-to-many — a test
  can appear under more than one parent, or under none), wired into
  `getTreeItem` (collapsible state) and `getChildren`.
- New icon: a dedicated glyph for the `test` dev-artifact kind, matching
  the pattern `STEP-000002-UVqkd7cL` set for `step`.
- `packages/catalyst-ui`: `NodeDetail.tsx`'s generic field/section
  rendering already renders a test's own detail view, and `<NodeList>`
  (`upstream`/`downstream`) already lists a test under its parent
  requirement's/step's "Produces (downstream)" once the graph edge
  exists — one added `NodeDetail` test case confirms this for a test
  node specifically.
- Added test coverage: `packages/catalyst-host-vscode/src/test/tree.test.ts`,
  `treeLabel.test.ts`, and `detail.test.ts` (Tests sub-section grouping,
  status glyph/icon rendering, and a requirement's/step's downstream
  list including a linked test, resolved via `reverseEdges`); one case
  in `catalyst-ui`'s `NodeDetail.test.ts`.

